From: Tabor SPE port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] debian/control: take javahelper for the build architecture

javahelper is Architecture: all without Multi-Arch: foreign, so a cross
build cannot satisfy it for the host architecture. It runs on the build
machine (like default-jdk:native and nasm:native in 0001), so qualify it
:native. Native builds are unchanged.

--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
                debhelper-compat (= 13),
                default-jdk:native [!hppa !hurd-any !powerpc !powerpcspe],
                help2man,
-               javahelper,
+               javahelper:native,
                nasm:native,
                libjpeg-turbo-progs:native (= 1:2.1.5-4) <cross>,
 Rules-Requires-Root: no
